{"name":"Winds Breath","hex":"#e0e1da","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winds","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wind"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of wind"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winds"},{"term":"breath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or process of breathing.","A single act of breathing in or out; a breathing of air."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["voiceless, surd; contrasting with voice (breath sounds, voice sounds)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind","wikidata":"Q8094"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/500px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/500px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cherry tree moving with the wind blowing about 22 m/sec (about 79 km/h or 49 mph)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif"},{"srcset":"htt